-- title:
--   Finite-law interface and binary machine primitives
-- statement:
--   The fixed-family transport law is expressed as a probability law on the platform finite space, with independent fair-bit padding and the corresponding public parameter data. Binary machine programs implement composition, list framing, integer arithmetic, Gaussian approximations, activation probabilities, and the body kernel. Their encodings expose an actual finite computation on input strings and random bits.
-- source:
--   Companion Lean implementation for the fixed-family Gaussian affine transport theorem. The source modules and their SHA-256 hashes are recorded in the checked extraction manifest. This exact generated file has SHA-256 dbb3c3ca2947702b40282eed380c81e114b9aca6b626a4f452c35f2c824a1a7d. Source modules: Integration9_9_CurrentZeroFiber, Integration9_9_CurrentAffineLaw, Integration9_9_FairBitPadding, Integration9_9_ActualSamplerLaw, Integration9_9_Parameters, Integration9_9_FixedFamilySamplerLaw, Integration9_9_TM2OutputLength, Integration9_9_TM2Simulation, Integration9_9_TM2Composition, Integration9_9_TM2BinaryAddition, Integration9_9_TM2AdditionFrontend, Integration9_9_TM2PairUnframe, Integration9_9_TM2BinaryComparison, Integration9_9_TM2Canonical, Integration9_9_TM2OutputEncoding, Integration9_9_TM2DynamicIntegerEncoding, Integration9_9_TM2NativeArithmetic, Integration9_9_TM2NativeFiniteSeries, Integration9_9_TM2NativeGaussian, Integration9_9_TM2NativeGaussianWindow, Integration9_9_TM2NativeActivation, Integration9_9_TM2NativePrime, Integration9_9_TM2NativeSliceProbability, Integration9_9_TM2NativeBodyKernel. Alternate sparse native dependencies preserve the original non-import body bytes and all public types; this header-only packaging is recorded in sparse_live/manifest.json. Current source SHA256 81cb9c1fbe604ed21a36a63555f91d514c774609dc29da68f714b061bb4a704f. Native10/11 split fallback keeps every original scope-closed data body unchanged and retains the canonical module names as import facades. Current source SHA256 81cb9c1fbe604ed21a36a63555f91d514c774609dc29da68f714b061bb4a704f.

